This was my second ascension, after the wizard Gamma.

>From reading this group, I think it was probably a pretty ordinary
valk ascension.  Flange found the grave of one of her predecessors in
the shallow mines.  It contained a magic marker and a cloak of magic
resistance, as well as plenty of food.

The minetown altar was co-aligned, and yielded magicbane without too
many problems.

Sokoban was easy enough thanks to Elbereth.  The bag of holding hidden
at the top came in handy.

On level 12 of the dungeon Flange found an altar and sat on it.  She
was granted a wish, and asked for +2 silver dragon scale mail.  Fort
Ludios was easy with the new armour.

Then she went to the quest, which was also easy.  

After the quest Flange returned to the first level of Sokoban to
reverse genocide some nurses.  She then returned to minetown, the only
available altar at this point, for some alchemy.

Level 16 was a more primitive world.

There was an altar on level 22.

Medusa was hiding on Level 25.

Gehennom was very boring, but she did find a magic lamp which she
blessed and used as a light source.  After finding the vibrating
square and digging passages between all the stairs (but before
fighting the wizard for the book) Flange went back up to the deepest
altar (level 22) for some more alchemy.  Then she went to level 1 and
dropped off all of her gold.

After defeating the wizard she found a second wand of wishing on the
bottom level of the dungeon.  Only the second time I've found a wand
of wishing outside the castle.  Too bad it's pretty useless by this
point.

The ascension run was a pain - got pulled back many, many times.  Also
had real trouble with the planes of earth and of fire, as Flange
couldn't find the portals.

Wished for a cockatrice corpse on the Astral Plane.  Went left but
that wasn't it.  Tried for the middle one - second time lucky!


